## Eligibility and interruption contract

Synthetic medication exclusions are baseline Bernoulli(.05); comorbidity prompts documented review rather than automatic efficacy ranking. Any L coordinate >3, adverse symptom, suspected infection/fever, confusion/fall, admission, regimen/steroid change or clinician concern creates a clinical-review/hold trigger. Only clinician-reviewed current eligibility can permit medication or experiment actions; synthetic numeric thresholds do not replace interaction/contraindication/fall-risk checks. Death ends outcomes; admission suspends decisions. No post-death ISI is generated. Day42 returns separate survival, hospitalization-by42, alive-outpatient probability, and each intervention's own conditional ISI and denominator/event times, exactly as accepted EST-INT. Zero conditioning probability is undefined. Do not interpret survivors as a common principal stratum or combine outcomes into a utility/winner.

